  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Gilding is the Promenade Ward's first major trade festival established after the Orca Incursion, held during the Frozen Peace. It marks the resumption of cargo movement between Aurora Stack surface merchants and Nightshelf fire-core suppliers through corridors that still bear scorch-marks from the siege. The festival's name references the tide-carved warehouses of the Promenade Ward — the same structures the orcas nearly breached — which merchant-guilds open when the aurora burns steady enough to justify the risk.
    
    ## Structure and Significance
    
    Aurora Stack traders arrange crystalline goods in light-catching displays; Nightshelf merchants stack fire-cores with characteristic efficiency. The Shell Hatch, a deep-tunneling technique that enabled safer subterranean transit, made Gilding's scale feasible — without it, the Nightshelf could not have moved sufficient fire-cores to warrant the venture.
    
    Several governing instruments were amended to accommodate the festival. The Tide Custom now governs its timing. The Circle Gathering, Aurora Stack's seasonal convocation, restructured its council logistics around Gilding's cycles. The Long-dark Edict, already layered with decades of crisis amendments, was further revised to permit extended merchant-watches. Even the Thaw-Kept emergency provisions were commemorated in its observance.
    
    During the third Gilding, the Radiant Ring — an artifact-weapon sealed within Aurora Stack — was publicly displayed but not activated.
    
    ## Character
    
    The festival is quieter than early accounts project. Memorial-tokens left at warehouse edges outnumber celebration-tokens. The old songs are not sung. There is cargo movement, shared rations, and a dark joke that circulates reliably: *'At least the orcas didn't take the ice itself.'*
